    "text_delta": "putational risk:** Risk modelling in banking is a relatively small, highly networked community. Raising allegations of bias based solely on the gender of the panel members can severely damage your professional reputation across peer institutions.\n* **Burning bridges:** Being shortlisted among the top three means you were considered a very strong contender. You may well be considered for future executive roles or reorganizations at this bank if you maintain a constructive relationship.\n\n---\n\n### Recommended Next Steps\n\n1. **Send a polite follow-up:** Reach out to the talent acquisition lead or recruiter with a brief, professional note:\n   > *\"I wanted to follow up on my request for feedback regarding the Head of Risk Modelling role. As I value the time spent with the team, any constructive insights on areas where I could strengthen my profile for future senior leadership opportunities would be greatly appreciated.\"*\n2. **Focus your questions on strategic gaps:** If you receive a call or written response, ask specifically what priorities the bank had for the role (e.g., immediate regulatory interactions, organizational restructuring) to understand how their strategic focus tipped the balance.\n3. **Keep the door open:** Express appreciation for reaching the final stage and reiterate your continued interest in senior opportunities with the firm.\n",
